          "where": "ops/devlane/dispatch/tests/test_launch_graft.py:236,249,276; ops/devlane/harness/tests/test_graft_query.py:426",
          "claim": "verify_worker/resume custody is proven only through the descriptor digest. Every negative test mutates the descriptor file or passes a stale meta.sha256, so a digest-only check (sha256(descriptor)==record.brief.graft.sha256) refuses. The contract's other three arms \u2014 installation pin, canonical snapshot (relocation), allowed cache location \u2014 are never presented as a valid-digest-but-foreign context, so an implementation that borrows another job's cache, a relocated snapshot, or a swapped GRAFT_INSTALL stays green.",
          "reproduce": "python3 -m unittest discover -s ops/devlane/dispatch/tests -p 'test_launch_graft.py'"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p3",
          "where": "ops/devlane/harness/tests/test_graft_query.py:156",
          "claim": "test_two_roots_do_not_share_a_cache supplies explicit distinct --cache paths, so caches differ by operator input, not by the default cache-key rule. The contract's real anti-sharing property ('a Git common directory or branch name is not a cache key; no worktree sharing') is unexercised: linked worktrees of one repo are never created, so a default cache keyed on the git common directory leaks one job's graph to another while staying green.",
          "reproduce": "python3 -m unittest test_graft_query.FreshnessAndCorruption -v"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p3",
          "where": "ops/devlane/harness/tests/test_graft_install.py:140",
          "claim": "test_probe_without_a_real_provider sets GRAFT_INSTALL=\"\" (the disabled config, which the status test demands report state 'disabled') yet asserts probe output contains 'unavailable'. A contract-faithful disabled probe refuses graft-disabled, whose line need not contain 'unavailable', so a correct impl fails; the test conflates disabled with unavailable and never exercises the native 'enabled-but-unmeasurable provider -> unavailable, never silently green' discipline.",
          "reproduce": "python3 -m unittest test_graft_install.ProbeIsUnavailableNotSilentlyGreen -v"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p3",
          "where": "ops/devlane/harness/tests/test_graft_query.py:292,306,319",
          "claim": "The truncated/wrong-type/provider-error prepare faults assert refusal, empty stdout and that the fake ran, but none assert the cache/binding was not published. The contract requires a failed prepare to leave no receipt and 'never residue'; the install-side partial test checks cache absence but these query-side fault tests do not, so an impl that mkdir/writes a partial graph before validating the provider result and then refuses stays green.",
          "reproduce": "python3 -m unittest test_graft_query.FreshnessAndCorruption.test_truncated_provider_response_is_graft_provider -v"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p3",
          "where": "ops/devlane/harness/tests/test_graft_install.py:37",
          "claim": "test_install_is_the_only_cli_verb_that_would_fetch guards 'only install downloads/invokes npm' by checking a hard-coded 'fresh' dir is absent and the literal 'npm' is not in status output. Absence of a directory name and a word is not absence of a fetch; an impl whose status shelled to the network without printing 'npm' passes. Proxy assertion, not a no-fetch guard.",
          "reproduce": "python3 -m unittest test_graft_install.InstallRefusesBeforeOverwrite.test_install_is_the_only_cli_verb_that_would_fetch -v"
        }
